## Argument forms

- `/<tool-name> <subcommand>` → runs `<tool> <subcommand>` and returns its output.
- `/<tool-name> "<natural-language request>"` → translates into the closest recipe above; if
  ambiguous, asks before running.

## Hard rules

- Allowlists `Bash(<tool> *)` only — won't run other commands without a separate prompt.
- Destructive `<tool>` subcommands (`delete`, `destroy`, `drop`, …) require an explicit confirmation
  in the user's prompt; don't infer them from context.
- If `<tool>` isn't installed, fail clearly with the install instruction (don't silently exit).
- For long-running commands, surface progress; don't swallow stderr.

